import type { Unit } from "@/content/types";

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// b2-unit-59-advanced-abstract-concepts — "Naming the Unnameable"
// Vocabulary-domain unit: a deeper, more specialized layer of abstract
// vocabulary than b2-unit-34-abstract-ideas. That unit teaches general
// philosophy/civic nouns (coscienza, identità, valore, libertà, giustizia,
// uguaglianza, società, benessere, felicità, significato/senso, verità,
// etica) paired with correlative grammar (anche se, più...più, sia...che,
// né...né, o...o, infinito come soggetto). This unit does not re-teach any
// of those exact words as new tier-1 cards; it goes one layer deeper into
// four specific clusters — consciousness/perception, paradox/contradiction,
// ambiguity/ambivalence, and identity/subjectivity — introducing genuinely
// new vocabulary (percezione, paradosso, contraddizione, ambivalenza,
// ambiguità, soggettività, and their word families) not present in b2-34.
// No overlap check needed against b2-unit-58-untranslatable-terms either:
// that unit's scope is discourse particles (boh, mah, dai, insomma...) and
// culturally-specific social concepts (sprezzatura, campanilismo, furbizia,
// bella figura...) — a different lexical territory entirely from the
// philosophical/psychological register taught here.
// No new grammar concept: tier 2 reinforces congiuntivo (opinion/doubt),
// relative pronouns (ciò che/quello che/il che), concessive clauses
// (sebbene/nonostante/anche se), si-impersonale/passivante, infinito
// sostantivato, and adjective agreement — all already taught in the B1/B2
// prerequisite chain — in fresh context built from this unit's new words.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

